  "<section class=\"course-page\" id=\"lesson-10\" data-chapter11-complete=\"brain\" hidden=\"\">\n<div class=\"p2-topic\">\n<header class=\"page-header\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-818\">Learn \u00b7 Chapter 11</p>\n<h1 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-819\">The brain</h1>\n<p class=\"lesson-question\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-820\">Where are the main brain structures, and what do they do?</p>\n<div class=\"goal-strip\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-01\">Learning goal</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-02\">I can identify the main brain structures and explain their functions.</p></div>\n<div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-03\">Before you begin</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-04\">Remember: the brain and spinal cord make up the CNS.</p></div></div>\n<details class=\"page-guide\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-summary\"><strong>How to complete this lesson</strong> \u2014 Learn \u2192 practise \u2192 required check \u2192 finish</summary>\n<div>\n<ol>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-01\"><strong>Start with the lesson.</strong> Read the learning goal and \u201cBefore you begin,\u201d then work through the explanation, diagrams and examples below. The embedded textbook is optional support: open it when you want another explanation or a closer look at a figure.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-02\"><strong>Use the learning goal and starting reminder.</strong> The learning goal above tells you what you must be able to explain. Read \u201cBefore you begin\u201d next to connect this lesson to what you already know.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-03\"><strong>Work through the online lesson in order.</strong> Read each teaching section and study its diagrams, examples and comparisons. Select an underlined biology term when you need its meaning. Use the video or Vocabulary help when an idea is still unclear.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-04\"><strong>Complete the required chapter check.</strong> Open the check near the bottom and select Start. For multiple choice, select Check answer; a correct answer unlocks the related writing. Answer in your own words and select Save written response for every response box.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-05\"><strong>Submit only when the required work is complete.</strong> Check that every required item has been attempted and every written response is saved. Then select Submit and finish. This stops the timer, records the completed run in All My Work and updates chapter progress.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-06\"><strong>Use optional practice only when it helps.</strong> Optional source practice and Practice &amp; Review activities can help you study, but they do not count toward the 12 required chapter checks.</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-guide-07\"><strong>Expected work:</strong> complete the lesson and submit the required chapter check. Use optional reading, videos and practice when they help. Drafts save automatically as you work in this browser.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n<div class=\"textbook-band\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-05\">Optional embedded reading</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-06\"><strong>Chapter 11 \u00b7 pp. 389\u2013392</strong></p></div><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"30\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-07\">Open at p. 389</a></div>\n<p class=\"lesson-term-strip\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-teacher-voice-terms\"><strong>Key terms:</strong> cerebrum \u00b7 cerebellum \u00b7 medulla oblongata \u00b7 pons \u00b7 thalamus \u00b7 hypothalamus</p>\n<details class=\"lesson-vocabulary-help\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-teacher-voice-vocab-summary\">Vocabulary help</summary>\n<section class=\"lesson-words\" aria-labelledby=\"lesson-10-anchor-words\"><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-08\">Key terms</p><h2 id=\"lesson-10-anchor-words\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-09\">Words for this lesson</h2><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-10\">Use these definitions when you need help with a term.</p><dl>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"hypothalamus\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-10\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-11\">hypothalamus</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-12\">a brain region that regulates internal conditions and links with the endocrine system</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"pituitary\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-10\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-13\">pituitary</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-14\">an endocrine gland connected to the hypothalamus</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"evidence\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-10\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-15\">evidence</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-16\">observations or results used to support an explanation</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"claim\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-10\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-17\">claim</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-18\">a statement or conclusion that can be checked</dd></div>\n</dl></section>\n<details class=\"lesson-term-inventory\"><summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-19\">More vocabulary for this lesson</summary><div><section aria-labelledby=\"lesson-10-all-terms\"><h3 id=\"lesson-10-all-terms\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-20\">Brain structures and reasoning terms</h3><dl><div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-21\">cerebrum \u00b7 cerebral cortex \u00b7 corpus callosum \u00b7 frontal lobe \u00b7 parietal lobe \u00b7 temporal lobe \u00b7 occipital lobe \u00b7 thalamus \u00b7 hypothalamus \u00b7 pituitary \u00b7 cerebellum \u00b7 medulla oblongata \u00b7 pons \u00b7 midbrain \u00b7 claim \u00b7 evidence</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-setup-22\">Select an underlined term for its definition. Your vocabulary writing is saved in Process Collection.</dd></div></dl></section></div></details>\n</details>\n</header>\n",
