  "\n<div class=\"content-section\">\n<section class=\"video-support\" data-video=\"q8NtmDrb_qo\">\n<h3 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-869\">Introduction to the brain</h3>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-870\">As you watch: Locate the major regions before trying to recall their functions. Keep the brainstem and cerebellum distinct.</p>\n<div data-video-slot=\"\">\n</div>\n<button type=\"button\" data-load-video=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-871\">Load video</button> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q8NtmDrb_qo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-872\">Watch on YouTube</a>\n<p class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-873\">Video not playing? Use the written explanation on this page.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"video-support\" data-video=\"0-8PvNOdByc\">\n<h3 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-874\">Structures of the brain: first recap</h3>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-875\">As you watch: Point to a structure, say its name, and state one function before continuing.</p>\n<div data-video-slot=\"\">\n</div>\n<button type=\"button\" data-load-video=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-876\">Load video</button> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0-8PvNOdByc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-877\">Watch on YouTube</a>\n<p class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-878\">Video not playing? Use the written explanation on this page.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"video-support\" data-video=\"jYlxv9gUYSs\">\n<h3 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-879\">Structures of the brain: second recap</h3>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-880\">As you watch: Distinguish the cerebrum, cerebellum, brainstem, thalamus and hypothalamus.</p>\n<div data-video-slot=\"\">\n</div>\n<button type=\"button\" data-load-video=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-881\">Load video</button> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jYlxv9gUYSs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-882\">Watch on YouTube</a>\n<p class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-883\">Video not playing? Use the written explanation on this page.</p>\n</section>\n</div>\n<details class=\"activity-disclosure\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-check-toggle\">Open chapter check: The brain</summary>\n<section class=\"activity\" data-activity=\"check-brain\" data-activity-mode=\"paired\" data-required-check=\"\">\n<h2 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-884\">Check: The brain</h2>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-885\">Chapter check \u00b7 Select Start when ready. The elapsed timer includes breaks; Submit and finish stops it. Redo preserves earlier attempts.</p>\n<div class=\"save-row\">\n<button type=\"button\" data-start=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-886\">Start</button>\n<output data-timer=\"\">Not started</output>\n</div>\n<fieldset data-run-body=\"\" disabled=\"\">\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"check-brain-mc\">\n<h3 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-887\">Which part of the brain is primarily responsible for controlling balance, posture, and coordination?</h3>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-888\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-brain-mc\" value=\"QUES_51662_82704_A275450\" data-answer=\"\"> pons</label>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-889\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-brain-mc\" value=\"QUES_51662_82704_A275451\" data-answer=\"\"> medulla oblongata</label>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-890\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-brain-mc\" value=\"QUES_51662_82704_A275452\" data-answer=\"\"> cerebral cortex</label>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-891\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-brain-mc\" value=\"QUES_51662_82704_A275453\" data-answer=\"\"> cerebellum</label>\n<button type=\"button\" data-check=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-892\">Check answer</button>\n<p data-feedback=\"\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-893\">\n</p>\n<fieldset class=\"paired-writing\" data-unlock=\"check-brain-mc\" disabled=\"\">\n<legend>Explain the related idea</legend>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-894\">\nIdentify the major structures in the hindbrain, midbrain, and forebrain, and the functions of these structures. </p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-895\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"30\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-896\">Textbook p. 389</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"check-brain-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-897\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"check-brain-written\" data-writing=\"check-brain-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"check-brain-written-limit check-brain-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"check-brain-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-898\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-899\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"check-brain-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-900\">\n</p>\n</fieldset>\n</div>\n</fieldset>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-run=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-901\">Submit and finish</button> <button type=\"button\" data-redo=\"\" hidden=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-902\">Redo activity</button>\n<p data-run-status=\"\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-903\">\n</p>\n</section>\n</details>\n<details class=\"activity-disclosure\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l10-practice-toggle\">Open optional source practice: The brain</summary>\n<section class=\"activity\" data-activity=\"practice-brain\" data-activity-mode=\"writing\">\n<h2 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-904\">Source practice: The brain</h2>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-905\">Optional source practice \u00b7 Select Start when ready. The elapsed timer includes breaks; Submit and finish stops it. Redo preserves earlier attempts.</p>\n<div class=\"save-row\">\n<button type=\"button\" data-start=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-906\">Start</button>\n<output data-timer=\"\">Not started</output>\n</div>\n<fieldset data-run-body=\"\" disabled=\"\">\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-checkpoint-21\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-907\">\nIdentify five homeostatic functions of the brain. </p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-908\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"30\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-909\">Textbook p. 389</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-checkpoint-21-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-910\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-checkpoint-21-written\" data-writing=\"source-checkpoint-21-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-checkpoint-21-written-limit source-checkpoint-21-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-checkpoint-21-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-911\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-912\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-checkpoint-21-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-913\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-checkpoint-23\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-914\">\nIdentify the four lobes of the cerebrum, and describe the function of each. </p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-915\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"33\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-916\">Textbook p. 392</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-checkpoint-23-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-917\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-checkpoint-23-written\" data-writing=\"source-checkpoint-23-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-checkpoint-23-written-limit source-checkpoint-23-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-checkpoint-23-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-918\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-919\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-checkpoint-23-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-920\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-checkpoint-24\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-921\">\nDescribe the primary areas of the brain that are responsible for the fine motor control of the muscles, as well as the area that processes sensory information from the skin. </p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-922\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"33\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-923\">Textbook p. 392</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-checkpoint-24-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-924\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-checkpoint-24-written\" data-writing=\"source-checkpoint-24-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-checkpoint-24-written-limit source-checkpoint-24-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-checkpoint-24-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-925\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-926\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-checkpoint-24-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-927\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-checkpoint-25\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-928\">\nCompare the locations and functions of Broca\u2019s area and Wernicke\u2019s area in the brain. </p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-929\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"33\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-930\">Textbook p. 392</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-checkpoint-25-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-931\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-checkpoint-25-written\" data-writing=\"source-checkpoint-25-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-checkpoint-25-written-limit source-checkpoint-25-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-checkpoint-25-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-932\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-933\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-checkpoint-25-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-934\">\n</p>\n</div>\n</fieldset>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-run=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-935\">Submit and finish</button> <button type=\"button\" data-redo=\"\" hidden=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-936\">Redo activity</button>\n<p data-run-